  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AZE: Support Azerbaijan to develop Carbon Market</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to support key stakeholders in Azerbaijan, the government and industry, to engage, inform and spark discussion on the main policies and tools to combat climate change and build the foundations for long term progress.
As part of its climate action, Azerbaijan is in the process of adopting carbon market legislation and possible tax incentives for greener companies. This will establish carbon compliance market that will control supply of carbon credits, regulate their trading, and incentivise companies to adopt a more sustainable business approach. 
Project activities will include:
1. Two (2) seminars, for 50-100 participants each, to raise awareness of carbon markets, carbon credit verification and UK carbon border adjustment mechanisms (CBAM) 
2. One-day roundtable discussion targeting policymakers, environmental policy, COP29 organisation committee, as well as business leaders, to highlight policy issues relevant to efforts to set foundations for carbon market infrastructure.  
3. 5-day training course</narrative>
  </description>
